## Simplified plan
Backend (Convex, new table `feedback`): `{clientId (uuid idempotency key), deviceId, text (1..2000), createdAt, receivedAt, context?: any (â‰¤8 KB), status: "received"|"looking"|"fixed", note?: string, updatedAt}`; indexes by_device [deviceId, createdAt], by_client [deviceId, clientId]. `feedback.submit` mutation (idempotent on deviceId+clientId; schedules an internal action), `feedback.listForDevice` query (newest 50, no context/deviceId), `feedback.setStatus` internal mutation the founder runs from the dashboard function runner ({id, status, note?} â†’ bumps updatedAt), `feedback.notify` internal action that emails the founder via the Resend REST API (env RESEND_API_KEY + FEEDBACK_EMAIL_TO already set; from onboarding@resend.dev; plain-text body with the text + a whitelisted context block; never deviceId; no retries).
Client: one composer sheet (text box + Send; "Includes this reminder's details" line when opened from a reminder) reachable from (a) a Settings row "Send feedback", (b) the failed-take card, (c) the reminder edit sheet ("Report a problem" â€” does not save or discard the user's unsaved edits). No email field. Context attached automatically: kind, reminder title/spoken line/schedule (from the store row â€” current values), errorKind/serverErrorCode/creationId/sttSource for failed takes, buildNumber, updateId, iOS version, timezone, local time. Durable AsyncStorage outbox (`lib/feedbackOutbox.ts`): persist first â†’ "Saved. Sends next time Remi is online." â†’ flush on app foreground/reconnect/after submit â†’ "Sent" only after the mutation returns. Status view: Settings â†’ "Your feedback" list from `listForDevice` (status chip Received / Looking into it / Fixed + note). On app open, if any item's `updatedAt` is newer than the locally stored last-seen timestamp, show a one-line banner "Your feedback was updated" that opens the list; tapping/opening marks it seen (local).

## Questions
- Q1: Is `updatedAt`-vs-local-last-seen the right "attended to" signal, or should the server carry a per-item `seenByUserAt`? (Two devices are not a case here â€” one device per user.)
- Q2: Reactivity â€” a `useQuery(listForDevice)` mounted at app root for the banner is one live subscription for the whole app life; acceptable, or gate it (subscribe only when the outbox has ever sent something, i.e. a local "hasFeedback" flag)?
- Q3: The edit-sheet entry: the sheet already has title/spoken-line/schedule inputs and a Save button. Where would a user expect "Report a problem" (a row under the schedule, or in the â‹¯/delete area) so it is not mistaken for Save/Delete?
- Q4: Anything in the App Store privacy labels or the privacy policy (legal-site/privacy.html) that this simplified version still changes, given no email is collected and the text is user-provided content tied to a device id?
